      "description": "Watch Dinamo Zagreb vs Kauno Žalgiris highlights and goals from UEFA Champions League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 4, 2026. The atmosphere was electric on August 4, 2026, as Dinamo Zagreb hosted Kauno Žalgiris in a high-stakes UEFA Champions League encounter. Both sides entered the pitch with massive European ambitions, setting the stage for a compelling night of continental football. A Lightning Double Strike The encounter began with high intensity, but it was the 32nd minute that truly broke the deadlock. Miha Zajc found the back of the net after a precise pass from Luka Stojkovic , sending the home crowd into a frenzy. Before the visitors could even regroup, Dinamo Zagreb struck again just sixty seconds later. Scott McKenna capitalized on a delivery from Matteo Perez Vinloef to double the lead, leaving Kauno Žalgiris stunned by the rapid-fire sequence of events. Maintaining the Momentum The second half saw no dip in the home side's aggression. In the 50th minute, Mateo Lisica further extended the advantage to 3-0, finishing off a move orchestrated by Josip Misic . As the game progressed, tactical substitutions brought fresh energy to the pitch, including the introduction of Mislav Orsic . The veteran winger made his mark in the 76th minute, providing the assist for Luka Stojkovic to claim a well-deserved goal and put the result beyond any doubt. Late Flourish and Final Whistle As the match entered its final stages, the visitors struggled to contain the pressure, leading to a yellow card for Anthony Kalik in the 85th minute. Dinamo Zagreb remained relentless until the very end. In the fourth minute of stoppage time, Lukas Kacavenda added a fifth goal following another brilliant setup by Josip Misic . The final whistle confirmed a comprehensive performance from the hosts, marking a dominant chapter in their European campaign."
